course: dictionary
lesson: 1692
title: Describing words and kindness
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Chubby means slightly fat and round in a soft, often cute way. You can see it in «chubby cheeks» and «a chubby baby». Picture something soft, round and cuddly.
explain: Context helps you see how the word works. «Squeeze a clump of wet moss from a wall into a dish and under a microscope you may see water bears, tiny eight-legged tardigrades plodding about like chubby bears in slow motion.» The tiny creatures look round and slow, so chubby is a picture word.
explain: Words about bodies can hurt. «xiǎo pàngzi» means chubby, or little fatty. A granny saying it to a toddler is praise, but a child saying it to another child is teasing, and that is not friendly. The same word can feel different depending on who says it.
explain: Before you describe a person, ask yourself: would this be kind? If you are not sure, choose a different word or describe something else.
fact: Chubby means slightly fat and round in a soft, often cute way.
fact: «Chubby cheeks» and «a chubby baby» are the usual ways we use it.
fact: Chubby is an adjective, so it can change: chubbier, chubbiest.
fact: Calling a person chubby can hurt them, so think before you say it.
fact: The Chinese word «xiǎo pàngzi» means chubby, and it can be praise or teasing depending on who says it.
exercise: «She had chubby cheeks and a big gap-toothed grin.» What does chubby mean here? | Very thin and pale | Loud and cheerful | Dirty from playing outside | *Slightly fat and round in a soft, cute way
exercise: «...tardigrades plodding about like chubby bears in slow motion.» What does plodding mean? | Swimming quickly | *Walking slowly and heavily | Flying very fast | Jumping high
exercise: Which word is the form of chubby that compares two things? | chubbiest | chubbily | chubbiness | *chubbier
test: Why can the same word feel kind from a granny but hurtful from a child? | Because grannies speak Chinese | Because it is always a rude word | *Because body teasing is not friendly, and who says it matters | Because toddlers cannot hear it
test: Which sentence uses chubby in a fond, cute way? | The chubby river ran fast. | *The chubby puppy snored by the fire. | The chubby sum was hard. | The chubby bus stopped at the corner.
exam: Someone says a friend is chubby, so the word must be rude. What is the best answer? | It is a colour | *It can describe a soft, round look, but calling someone chubby can still hurt, so think about kindness first | It is always rude, so never use it | It means very tall
